Subject: [PATCH] netifd: allow protocols to accept live configuration updates

Let an up ucode protocol opt into compatible configuration changes with a
pure config_update callback. Accepted configurations use the existing renew
queue and instance; other interface changes retain the full reload path.
Allow the protocol to retire old dependency watches after successful apply.

--- a/proto.h
+++ b/proto.h
@@ -59,6 +59,8 @@
 	/* filled in by the protocol handler */
 	int (*notify)(struct interface_proto_state *, struct blob_attr *data);
 	int (*cb)(struct interface_proto_state *, enum interface_proto_cmd cmd, bool force);
+	/* Accept a configuration update without tearing down the live instance. */
+	bool (*config_update)(struct interface_proto_state *, struct blob_attr *config);
 	void (*free)(struct interface_proto_state *);
 };
 
